      "cwe_id": [915],
      "note": "Preferences are a flat hash whose keys are 'channel:type' strings (e.g. 'email:any', 'in_app:welcome'). The PreferencesController#update method itself does the validation inline before any DB write: channel is checked against Notifications::NotificationPreference::CHANNELS (frozen engine-internal whitelist), type is regex-matched against /\\A[a-z0-9_]+\\z/ or 'any', and the value is coerced to a boolean (==\"1\"). Only the single :enabled column is touched on the row, via find_or_initialize_by + update!. permit! is used because the channel:type keyset is dynamic; an exhaustive permit() list would have to enumerate every pair. Re-evaluate if a future code path lets user input flow into the channels list."
    }
